---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CLARITY_ID, CONTACT_EMAIL, GA4_ID, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
const title = `Privacy policy – ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}`;
const description = GA4_ID ? 'Google Analytics audience measurement with cookies and no advertising; inputs kept in your browser; host logs; your rights and the supervisory authority.' : 'Inputs kept in your browser, no cookies, host logs: the data processing behind the site, your rights and the supervisory authority you can contact.';
---
{/* Page générée par scripts/gen-legal-pages.py (trame, décision GA4 du 2026-10-17). Ne pas
     retoucher à la main : relancer le script. Un passage propre au site se garde entre
     les marqueurs site:debut et site:fin. */}
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This page describes the processing of personal data linked to the use of {SITE_URL}, under Articles 12 to 14 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and, for visitors in New Zealand, the Privacy Act 2020.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>For any question about your data: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer has been appointed, as the conditions of Article 37 GDPR are not met.</p>
    <h2>2. What you type stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>The site’s calculations run in your browser. The amounts, dates and circumstances you enter <strong>are sent to no server</strong>, are stored nowhere and are linked to no identifier. The site asks for no account, name or email address. A share link carries your inputs in the page address: only send it to people you choose.</p>
    <h2>3. Processing carried out</h2>
    <h3>Host access logs</h3>
    <p>For each request the host records the IP address, date and time, the page requested, the browser and the referring page. Purpose: security of the service and fault diagnosis. Legal basis: the publisher’s legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; in New Zealand, Information Privacy Principle 1 of the Privacy Act 2020, collection for a lawful purpose connected with our activities). Retention: as set by the host’s own policy.</p>
    {GA4_ID ? (<>
    <h3>Audience measurement with Google Analytics</h3>
    <p>The site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages are useful: pages viewed, referring page, visit length, device and browser type, approximate country and city. To do so Google Analytics sets two cookies on your device: <code>_ga</code>, which tells visitors apart with a random identifier, and <code>_ga_{GA4_ID.replace('G-', '')}</code>, which keeps the state of the visit. Their lifetime is set to 13 months at most (390 days) and is not extended on each visit; Google’s default is 2 years.</p>
    <p>The IP address is anonymised: Google Analytics 4 neither logs nor stores it, and only uses it at collection time to derive an approximate country and city. The page address sent to Google Analytics is stripped of its parameters, so the inputs carried by a share link are not included. The site shows no advertising: ad storage, ad user data, ad personalisation and Google signals are switched off, and measurement data is shared with no advertiser.</p>
    <p>Purpose: audience measurement. Legal basis: the publisher’s legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; in New Zealand, Information Privacy Principle 1 of the Privacy Act 2020, collection for a lawful purpose connected with our activities). Provider: Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. Retention at Google: 14 months for visit-level and identifier-level data, then deletion; only anonymous totals remain.</p>
    </>) : (<>
    <h3>No audience measurement</h3>
    <p>The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics or advertising tool.</p>
    </>)}
    {CLARITY_ID && (<>
    <h3>Technical stability monitoring with Microsoft Clarity, cookie-free</h3>
    <p>To spot errors, slow pages and buttons that do not respond, the site uses Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode: Clarity sets no cookies, each page view gets its own identifier, and page text and your inputs are masked. Clarity receives the page structure, clicks, scrolling, device type, load times and errors. Purpose: site stability. Legal basis: the publisher’s legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; in New Zealand, Information Privacy Principle 1 of the Privacy Act 2020, collection for a lawful purpose connected with our activities). Provider: Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland. Retention: 30 days for page recordings, 13 months at most for aggregated data.</p>
    </>)}
    <h3>Messages you send us</h3>
    <p>If you write to the contact address, your email address and message are kept for as long as needed to reply and, where relevant, fix an error, then deleted no later than three years after the last exchange. Legal basis: the publisher’s legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR; in New Zealand, Information Privacy Principle 1 of the Privacy Act 2020, collection for a lawful purpose connected with our activities).</p>
    <h2>4. Recipients</h2>
    <p>No data is sold, rented or passed on. Access is limited to the host{GA4_ID && ', Google Ireland Limited for Google Analytics'}{CLARITY_ID && ', Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited for Clarity'}, acting as processors under Article 28 GDPR. No advertising network operates on the site.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>Host logs may be processed in the United States.{GA4_ID && ' Google Analytics data may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States.'}{CLARITY_ID && ' Clarity data may be transferred to Microsoft Corporation in the United States.'} These transfers rely on the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and portability set out in Articles 15 to 22 GDPR. Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we reply within one month. With no user accounts, we usually hold no data that identifies you, and we will tell you so.</p>
    {GA4_ID && (<p>To object to audience measurement without writing to us: block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The site works the same way.</p>)}
    {CLARITY_ID && (<p>For stability monitoring: block the <code>clarity.ms</code> domain in your browser or with a content blocker.</p>)}
    <p>You may lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority: {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>). In New Zealand you may also complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner.</p>
    <h2>7. No automated decision-making</h2>
    <p>A calculation result is an estimate produced at your request, from your inputs, in your browser. It has no legal effect and is not an automated decision under Article 22 GDPR. No profiling takes place.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page. Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
